//? Title: YOLO v3 residual features and global three-scale assignment
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Verify exact independent-logistic loss derivatives, global prior/scale matching and full80/20-class graphs, then visibly fit the complete compact75-convolution model with multiscale Adam, paired BN checkpoints and actual digit scenes.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.6_object_detection/yolo_v3.cpp`.

> The method

YOLO v3 combines residual Darknet53 features with three top-down prediction scales. A target selects one prior globally; independent class/objectness logistic losses and area-weighted coordinates train all scales in one visible tensor optimization loop.

The concept diagram below is drawn by `dm::graphics::Diagram`. Its editable C++
source is the complete block below; regeneration uses the same datamunge toolchain
as the numerical examples. Exports consume the saved local SVG.

```{cpp, file="figures/yolo_v3_concept.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::Diagram diagram;
  diagram.node("n0", {0.0, 0}, "Nine box priors\nOne global match");
  diagram.node("n1", {5.2, 0}, "Residual Darknet53\nThree scale heads");
  diagram.node("n2", {10.4, 0}, "Explicit Adam loop\nIndependent class BCE");
  diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
  diagram.save_svg("build/yolo_v3_concept.svg");
}
